# Feature notes (required)

The repo keeps developer docs in `notes/`. Each product feature has a markdown file covering **What**, **Why**, **How it works**, and **Developer details**.

## When you add or ship a new feature

1. Create `notes/NN-kebab-name.md` using `notes/_TEMPLATE.md` (next free number).
2. Fill What / Why / How / Key files / Env / Related links — do not leave a stub if you implemented the feature in this session.
3. Add a row to the index in `notes/README.md`.
4. If you only scaffolded code and the hook created a stub, upgrade the stub before finishing.

## When you change an existing feature

Update the matching `notes/*.md` if behavior, entry points, env vars, or data model changed.

## What counts as a feature

- New protected route/page (Dashboard, Overview, Q&A-style product surface)
- New `src/lib/*` domain module (GitHub/AI/meeting/etc.)
- New tRPC procedures that introduce user-facing capability
- New webhook/API route for a product pipeline

Not required for: pure UI polish, typo fixes, refactors with no behavior change, shadcn primitives.

## Naming

`NN-short-kebab-case.md` — e.g. `17-slack-digest.md`.
